  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to check the panels render, and the rule's status is still \"pending\" because it hasn't run yet.\n\n**Data:** the logs data view is `kibana_sample_data_logs`, with `timestamp` as its time field. Each document is a web request. The fields I used are the response code (`response` and `response.keyword`), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `host`, `machine.os`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-2d8f61df Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Requests by response code\n- Average bytes by extension\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-2d8f61df-web-logs-overview-b2dc17321402.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-2d8f61df 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It runs every minute. It fires when more than 10 documents have a `response.keyword` starting with \"5\" in the last 5 minutes. Its id is `af89b457-1253-4821-9b08-7317f1f5b110`. I didn't add any notification action, so it will only show up as an alert in Kibana.\n\nThe sample data's timestamps may not fall in the last 5 minutes, in which case the rule won't fire.",
